      "next_action": "Speak to Murli Boila  Further discussion with Nishit Shah",
      "director_message": ""
    },
    {
      "id": 139,
      "user_id": 9,
      "date": "2026-08-05",
      "client_name": "Cybercity Builders and Developers Pvt Ltd",
      "task_description": "[{\"date\":\"2026-08-05\",\"text\":\"Vizag Project 2  *2. Iconica Capital & Iconica Crown* This project is under Iconica Projects, a partnership firm where Garden City and Cyber City each hold a 50% stake. * It is an apartment project spanning 17 lakh sq. ft., of which 1 lakh sq. ft. is allocated to a third party, leaving 16 lakh sq. ft. as the developer’s share. * Out of this, 5 lakh sq. ft. has already been sold at ₹6,500 per sq. ft. * ₹120 crore has been received so far, with ₹220 crore receivable from sold inventory. * Unsold inventory has a potential receivable value of ₹800 crore. * Occupancy Certificate (OC) is expected in 3 years. * Total project cost is ₹575 crore, with Yelawati as the local contractor. * Existing loan from HDFC Bank stands at ₹117 crore. * An additional ₹100 crore is required for construction funding, making the total requirement ₹217 crore. They initially approached State Bank of India, but the proposal has not progressed. We can consider discussing this with Union Bank of India and also re-engage with SBI. Please note these details for further discussion.\"}]",
      "status": "in_progress",
      "priority": "medium",
